From b742567cc1573be237d4af0b57a7bde6110d6960 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 23:51:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(app): cross-hole entry welds a non-conforming round
 before its sag allowance

The per-line cross-hole entry (#85) thickens each stock/part facet by a
chord-sag allowance read from its edge neighbours, found by bit-near
(1e-6 mm quantised) vertices. A round exported with each facet carrying
its own, slightly different corner copies (a non-conforming STL) found
no neighbours, got no allowance, and was read at its chords: the hole
mouth up to the chord sag inside real metal, and the #84 shank reach
short by the same.

The allowance moves to its own module, cross_sag, and finds neighbours
by edge proximity: vertices are welded first within 1e-6 of the model's
bounding diagonal (floor 1e-9 mm) on a uniform grid hash (27-cell scan,
deterministic in input order, O(n)), and edges match on welded ids. A
genuinely open edge - no facet edge within the tolerance - still gets
no allowance. More allowance only moves the entry outward (air, never
metal).

Pinned by cross_entry::an_unwelded_round_is_entered_and_reached_as_the_welded_one
and cross_sag::an_unwelded_round_edge_carries_the_allowance_and_an_open_edge_none.

Fixes #121

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
